            "Yes, because the homeowner's oral agreement to the price increase created an enforceable modification upon delivery and acceptance of the chandelier.",
            "No, because the modification was procured in bad faith through an extortionate threat of economic breach without a legitimate commercial reason.",
            "No, because the modification violated the common law pre-existing duty rule."
